<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela gov't presents social security reforms.</title>
<headline>Venezuela gov't presents social security reforms.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan Ministers formally presented to Congress on Thursday a comprehensive bill to reform the county's cumbersome and outdated social security system.</p>
<p>The law, which covers health, housing, professional education, unemployment insurance and pensions, will be examined by five congressional sub-commissions.</p>
<p>Congress is currently examining proposed reforms of the Labor Law and severance pay system.  Once passed, the two complementary bills are expected to radically free-up Venezuela's rigid labor markets.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
</text>
